# Wave H.q — Operator wizard-calendar BEM

## Problem

After H.l.b / H.p, time + date + datetime chrome use `operator-*` BEM, but the **portal calendar grid** still brands every cell/nav/title as Denali:

- Classes: `.denali-wizard-calendar`, `__day`, `__nav`, `__picker-cell`, …
- Theme tokens: `--denali-wizard-calendar-primary*` (and hover/fg variants)

These are operator wizard chrome hooks scoped under `body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"]` — product skin, not product identity in the class name.

## Decision

Rename in lockstep (TSX + CSS + theme specs):

| Before | After |
| ------ | ----- |
| `denali-wizard-calendar` (+ elements/modifiers) | `operator-wizard-calendar` |
| `--denali-wizard-calendar-primary*` | `--operator-wizard-calendar-primary*` |

Keep `body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"]` selectors. Keep component file name `denali-calendar.tsx` / export names for a later package rename wave.

## Out of scope

- `.denali-wizard-composite` / `.denali-review*` / picker BEMs → review BEM **done in** [`wave-h-operator-review-bem.mdoc`](./wave-h-operator-review-bem.mdoc) (Wave H.r); composite/pickers remain
- Token colors (`denali-alpine-600`, `denali-forest-*`) — brand palette, not chrome
- Install-graph isolation

## Verify

```bash
rg 'denali-wizard-calendar' packages/workspaces/denali apps/web --glob '!**/*.generated.*'
# expect empty except ADR / forbid lists
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wave-h-operator-wizard-calendar-bem.spec.ts \
  test/denali-wizard-theme.spec.ts \
  test/wave-h-operator-datetime-bem.spec.ts
```
